            <ArticleTitle>Sleep effects on breathing and respiratory diseases.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>117-22</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.4103/0970-2113.56345</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>To understand normal sleep pattern and physiological changes during sleep, sleep and breathing interaction, nomenclature and scales used in sleep study, discuss the effect of rapid eye movements and non-rapid eye movements while sleep and to review the effects of obstructive and restrictive lung disease on gas exchange during sleep and sleep architecture.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
